From b9997bf2ae40e3b73ea55bbe8e212492d7422a84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 03:19:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] OpenGL patch

Allow the Cocoa OpenGL backend to build with the Mac OS X 10.5/10.6 SDK
and gcc, and fall back to a legacy (2.x) context when no core profile
is available.

Rebased onto 9.7.1. In addition to the previous changes, guard
-[NSOpenGLContext pixelFormat] in InitializeFromCurrentContext(): it
only exists on 10.10+, so on older systems derive the pixel format from
the CGL context instead of crashing with an unrecognized selector.
CGLGetPixelFormat() lives in OpenGL.framework, which the Cocoa backend
did not link before, so link it explicitly. It is 10.6+, so with a 10.5
deployment target the pixel format is left unset.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
